0 -16 Td
(1. Introduction) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Graph neural networks \(GNNs\) learn representations of nodes, edges and whole graphs by) Tj
0 -16 Td
(repeatedly exchanging information between neighbouring nodes. This process is called) Tj
0 -16 Td
(message passing. In each layer, every node aggregates messages from its neighbours,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(combines them with its own state, and applies a learned transformation.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(2. Graph Convolutional Networks) Tj
0 -16 Td
(A graph convolutional network \(GCN\) averages neighbour features using a symmetric) Tj
0 -16 Td
(normalisation based on node degrees, followed by a linear layer and a non-linearity.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Because every neighbour is weighted by a fixed coefficient, GCN layers are cheap to) Tj
0 -16 Td
(compute and work well on homophilous graphs where connected nodes share labels.) Tj
0 -16 Td
ET
endstream
