(Attention and Sampling) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -28 Td
(3. Graph Attention Networks) Tj
0 -16 Td
(A graph attention network \(GAT\) replaces the fixed coefficients of a GCN with learned) Tj
0 -16 Td
(attention weights. Each node scores its neighbours with a small attention function and) Tj
0 -16 Td
(normalises the scores with a softmax. Multiple attention heads are usually concatenated) Tj
0 -16 Td
(or averaged. Attention lets the model down-weight noisy or irrelevant neighbours.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(4. Neighbourhood Sampling) Tj
0 -16 Td
(GraphSAGE-style models sample a fixed number of neighbours per node instead of using the) Tj
0 -16 Td
(full neighbourhood. Sampling bounds memory use on very large graphs and enables) Tj
0 -16 Td
(inductive learning on nodes that were not seen during training.) Tj
0 -16 Td
ET
endstream
endobj
