(Limitations and Evaluation) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -28 Td
(5. Known Limitations of Message Passing) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Over-smoothing: as more layers are stacked, node representations become increasingly) Tj
0 -16 Td
(similar, which hurts classification accuracy in deep GNNs.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Over-squashing: information from distant nodes must pass through narrow bottlenecks,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(so long-range dependencies are compressed into fixed-size vectors.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Expressiveness: standard message passing is at most as powerful as the 1-WL graph) Tj
0 -16 Td
(isomorphism test, so some non-isomorphic graphs cannot be distinguished.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(6. Evaluation Practice) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Results on small citation benchmarks vary noticeably with the random seed. Reports should) Tj
0 -16 Td
(therefore give the mean and standard deviation over several seeds, state whether lower) Tj
0 -16 Td
(or higher values of each metric are better, and use the same data splits for every model.) Tj
0 -16 Td
ET
endstream
